# Help: The device mapper targets and features dm-targets leaves out
#
# Layered on storage/dm-targets.config: dm-verity, with forward error
# correction and signed root hashes, the zoned, emulated block size,
# switch, unstriped and inline encryption targets, the userspace
# mirror log, the I/O affinity path selector, and the audit and IMA
# events dm-mod sends. dm-mod builds its zoned device support,
# dm-zone.c, under BLK_DEV_ZONED.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - MD and BLK_DEV_DM, and DM_MIRROR and DM_MULTIPATH, which the
#   userspace log and the path selector extend.
# - BLK_DEV_ZONED for DM_ZONED, BLK_INLINE_ENCRYPTION for
#   DM_INLINECRYPT and AUDIT for DM_AUDIT.
# - IMA, on SECURITY and INTEGRITY, for dm-mod's IMA measurements.
#
# builtin/storage/dm-extras.config builds them in, with what needs
# dm-mod built in: dm-mod.create= (DM_INIT) and LoadPin's trust in
# dm-verity devices.
# See: drivers/md/Kconfig
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/device-mapper/index.html

#
# Inlined prerequisites
#
CONFIG_MD=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_DM=m
CONFIG_DM_MIRROR=m
CONFIG_DM_MULTIPATH=m
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_ZONED=y
CONFIG_BLK_INLINE_ENCRYPTION=y
CONFIG_AUDIT=y
CONFIG_SECURITY=y
CONFIG_INTEGRITY=y
CONFIG_IMA=y

#
# Targets
#
CONFIG_DM_VERITY=m
CONFIG_DM_VERITY_FEC=y
CONFIG_DM_VERITY_VERIFY_ROOTHASH_SIG=y
CONFIG_DM_ZONED=m
CONFIG_DM_EBS=m
CONFIG_DM_SWITCH=m
CONFIG_DM_UNSTRIPED=m
CONFIG_DM_INLINECRYPT=m
CONFIG_DM_LOG_USERSPACE=m
CONFIG_DM_MULTIPATH_IOA=m
CONFIG_DM_AUDIT=y
